Beth Friedman  <bjf@wavefront.com> wrote:
>I'd like to think that it's possible to get a decent wizard going
>without having to depend on an early wish or a really good bones pile.
>But that's the only way I've ever managed to ascend a wizard.

I've done one wizard, without any such luck, and also shunning Elbereth.
Things that seemed to work;

Use the pet. A magic whistle is a blessing in the early game, so is a
leash. Don't be afraid to burn food on taming pets - let your god deal
with starvation and your pets with monsters.

Identify all wands. Attack wands can save your bacon; so can WoSleep; so
can WoDigging.

Pet-ID and price-ID spellbooks as soon as possible.

Get telepathy and a blindfold/towel as soon as is feasible. Use it. If you
have a ring of warning at the start, use _that_.

Collect daggers. Thrown daggers are far more effective then your spells at
low levels, and the sooner you can raise dagger skill the better. You
don't have to carry much heavy armour; make use of this by carrying every
dagger you find so you never run out of ammo. Now you don't have to suck
your food away on force bolt, and can save your mana for more useful
spells.

Consider tolerating spell failure if you find an armour item with an
impressive bonus - a +4 orcish helm, say.
